OL,3,GNEWSAStone to be laid for Mobo founder
OL,4,AKanya King
OL,5,
OL,6,FA commemorative stone is to be laid in
OL,7,FLondon in honour of the late Mobo
OL,8,Ffounder Kanya King, to mark the 30th
OL,9,Fanniversary of the music ceremony.
OL,11,FThe Mobo awards music ceremony - which
OL,12,Fcelebrates black music, culture and
OL,13,Fexcellence from the UK and abroad - was
OL,14,Flaunched by King in 1996.
OL,16,FThrough Mobo, King is credited with
OL,17,Fplaying a major role in bringing black
OL,18,Fmusic and culture to the mainstream in
OL,19,Fthe UK. King died this summer from
OL,20,Fcolon cancer at the age of 57.
OL,23,APub: 05-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
